{
 "_meta": {
  "purpose": "Canonical names and places for Southern Arizona municipalities. Loaded by ai_reporter.py and injected into the news-report generation prompt to correct Deepgram mistranscriptions.",
  "last_updated": "2026-08-11",
  "deepgram_misreads_note": "Each known misread observed in a transcript should be added to the `deepgram_misreads` array. The pipeline will tell the LLM to replace any of these with the canonical form.",
  "verification_needed": [
   "regional.people: Suzanne Droubie (Pima County Assessor) — re-verify on pima.gov before relying on",
   "pima-county.people: Dan Hunt (CIO) — most recent direct confirmation was 2022; re-verify",
   "pima-county.people: pronouns unset for Carmine DeBonis Jr., Monica Perez, Art Cuaron, Jackson Jenkins, Dan Hunt — confirm on pima.gov before adding (do not infer from name)",
   "regional.people: pronouns unset for Suzanne Droubie, Joe Snell, Laurie Kierstead-Joseph, John Cross, JD Wallace",
   "pima-county.people: Michael Racy — Deepgram rendered as 'Rossi'/'Rask'; confirm current Pima County lobbying contract status",
   "pima-county.people: Sarah Feld — named aloud in the 2026-07-28 IDA appointment motion as the affiliated-nonprofits representative (term to 2028). Transcript-only, no external confirmation; deliberately NOT added as canonical. Confirm via Legistar minutes or Clerk of the Board.",
   "pima-county.people: Daniel Dempsey — nominated for Treasurer 2026-07-28 by Supervisor Cano (motion failed for lack of a second). Transcript-only spelling; withheld from the 2026-07-28 published report rather than printed unverified, same as Sarah Feld.",
   "pima-county.people: pronouns unset for Nancy Cole, Patrick DeConcini, John H. Payne, Kenneth M. Silverman, Diane Quihuis, Paul Kraft — do not infer from name.",
   "sahuarita.people: pronouns unset for John Sparks, Tony Bruno, Denise Reis, Raul Rodriguez, Amy Petersmarck, Manuel O. Valenzuela, Ed.D. — confirm on susd30.us before adding (do not infer from name)",
   "sahuarita.people: Tony Bruno — district site says 'Tony', roll call says 'Anthony Bruno'. Formal vs informal, NOT a misread; decide which form reports should use. Do not add 'Anthony' to deepgram_misreads.",
   "sahuarita.people: John Sparks — addressed as 'doctor John Sparks' at roll call; confirm the doctorate on susd30.us before putting Dr. in his title (transcript-only for now).",
   "sahuarita.people: Lisette Huey (Chief Financial Officer) and an unnamed assistant superintendent were called at the 2026-07-08 roll call but are NOT on susd30.us's leadership page as fetched. Transcript-only = hypothesis; verify before adding.",
   "marana.people: Dennis Shannon and Bennett Burke — members of the public who gave speaker cards 2026-08-04. Transcript-only spellings; confirm before printing a private citizen's name (Burke referenced an article he submitted to the Arizona Daily Star, which is externally checkable).",
   "marana: 'Seward Basin 20' (2026-08-04 wastewater item) — transcript-only, absent from the agenda and looks like a mangled development/basin name. Ear-check the recording before it appears in print.",
   "tucson.people: Roi Lusk — pronouns unset; 2026-08-05 transcript uses 'mister' honorific but the segment is garbled; confirm before adding (do not infer from name)",
   "tucson.people: Piroschka Glinsky — nickname rendered 'Perry/Peri' in the 2026-08-05 memorial; likely 'Piri' (Hungarian diminutive) but unconfirmed; do not print a nickname",
   "tucson.people: 2026-08-05 lesson — Mike Rankin was listed as City Attorney a year after his retirement, causing the drafter to 'correct' the transcript's accurate 'Lusk' into the stale 'Rankin'. Re-verify officeholders in this file on a schedule, not just misspellings.",
   "pima-county.people: Francisco Lopez -- pronouns unset; confirm on pima.gov before adding (do not infer from name)"
  ],
  "scope_note": "Regional bucket also holds state-level officials (e.g., Arizona Auditor General) since they appear at any municipality's meetings and don't belong in any single municipality bucket. School districts get their own bucket keyed on the slug prefix used by agenda_mining_sahuarita.py / ai_reporter.py (e.g. 'sahuarita').",
  "pronouns_note": "Pronouns are injected so the model does not infer gender from a name (root cause of a 2026-07-14 Pima County draft misgendering Supervisor Andrés Cano). Only add pronouns that are evidenced — transcript honorifics/pronoun use, or documented public record. If unknown, leave the field off and add the person to verification_needed rather than guessing."
 },
